  "title": "Dilbarjin",
  "provenance": "Barrington Atlas: BAtlas 98 G1 Dilbarjin",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/settlement"
  ],
  "details": "<p>P. Bernard, writing in Encyclopaedia Iranica (<a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/delbarjin\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">online</a>) notes that the city of \"Eukratideia\" mentioned by both Strabo (<a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://data.perseus.org/citations/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0099.tlg001.perseus-grc1:11.11.2\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">11.11.2</a>) and Ptolemy (<a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.39015022717584;view=1up;seq=125\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">6.11.8</a>) may, in fact, correspond to the site of\u00a0Dilbarjin in Bactria.</p>\r\n<p>\u00a0</p>\r\n<p><em>The Barrington Atlas Directory</em> notes: Dilbarjin, AFG</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Dilbarjin is an ancient city of northern Afghanistan. The site may have been founded under the Achaemenid Empire. Under the Kushan Empire, the site was a fortified local center of some importance.",
